# agentic Docker env — prefer the wizard:  ./docker/setup.sh  (it validates these).
# Copy to docker/.env and edit if writing by hand. PATHS + IDs only; all behavior
# (model, context budget, mode, API key) is set in the browser after startup.
#
# ── SAFETY MODEL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only two host paths are mounted, both narrow and identity-mapped:
#   AGENTIC_STATE_DIR — STATE only (queue/worktrees/diffs/logs/settings/secrets)
#   PROJECT_DIR       — the repo(s) you work on (what the UI picker can browse)
# They MUST be disjoint (neither inside the other), and AGENTIC_STATE_DIR must
# NOT be a source checkout. App source is baked in the image — never mounted.
# Use ABSOLUTE paths, no '~', no trailing slash.
#
# NOTE: the state var is AGENTIC_STATE_DIR, NOT AGENTIC_HOME — a native install
# exports AGENTIC_HOME in your shell, and Compose lets shell env override .env,
# so reusing that name would let your real ~/.agentic silently shadow this.

# STATE dir — keep it SEPARATE from your ~/.agentic source repo. Default is safe.
AGENTIC_STATE_DIR=/Users/you/.agentic-data

# Project repo, or a parent folder of repos. The ONLY host code the container
# sees; pick it NARROW — never your whole home dir. Examples:
#   single repo:     /Users/you/Projects/myapp
#   projects parent: /Users/you/Projects
PROJECT_DIR=/Users/you/Projects

# Host home dir (for Path.home() alignment). NOT mounted.
HOST_HOME=/Users/you

# So files created in the mounts stay owned by you. From: id -u  /  id -g
HOST_UID=501
HOST_GID=20

# Dashboard port (use 4081 if a native agentic already owns 4080).
HOST_PORT=4080

# Host's NATIVE Ollama. Start it with OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 so the container connects.
OLLAMA_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434
